WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:11.707
♪ ♪

00:00:10.472 --> 00:00:12.941
&gt;&gt; Shannon: DE DAY, THE SIXTH

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.010
OF JUNE.

00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:17.679
TODAY IS THE 74TH ANNIVERSARY OF

00:00:15.144 --> 00:00:19.748
THAT DAY, CONSIDERED THE TURNING

00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:20.749
POINT IN WORLD WAR II.

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:22.217
NATIONAL SECURITY CORRESPONDENT

00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:24.353
JENNIFER GRIFFIN SHOWS US HOW

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:27.423
IT'S BEING REMEMBERED.

00:00:24.486 --> 00:00:28.524
&gt;&gt; YOUR TASK WILL NOT BE AN EASY

00:00:27.556 --> 00:00:30.325
ONE.

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:30.959
YOUR ENEMY IS WELL-TRAINED,

00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:31.326
WELL-EQUIPPED, AND BATTLE

00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:32.194
HARDENED.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.229
HE WILL FIGHT SAVAGELY.

00:00:32.661 --> 00:00:34.763
WE WILL ACCEPT NOTHING LESS THAN

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:37.766
FULL VICTORY.

00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:38.434
&gt;&gt; WITH THOSE WORDS,

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.068
GENERAL DWIGHT D. EISENHOWER

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.904
LAUNCH THE D-DAY INVASION

00:00:39.201 --> 00:00:57.419
SENDING MORE THAN 156,000 ALLIED

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:57.419
TROOPS TO FRANCE TO FREE

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:02.558
SENDING MORE THAN 156,000 ALLIED

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:03.192
TROOPS TO FRANCE TO FREE EUROPE

00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:03.859
FROM NAZI GERMANY'S GRIP.

00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:04.226
MANY DIED ON THE BEACHES OF

00:01:03.992 --> 00:01:04.660
NORMANDY.

00:01:04.359 --> 00:01:05.394
JUNE 6, 1944.

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:06.095
VISITORS MARK THE ANNIVERSARY OF

00:01:05.527 --> 00:01:06.595
THE AMERICAN MILITARY CEMETERY

00:01:06.228 --> 00:01:07.262
ABOVE THE BEACHES.

00:01:06.728 --> 00:01:07.963
SOME WHO SURVIVED ATTENDED A

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:08.564
CEREMONY WREATH LAYING AT THE

00:01:08.097 --> 00:01:09.031
WORLD WAR II MEMORIAL IN

00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:09.231
WASHINGTON, D.C.

00:01:09.164 --> 00:01:09.231
&gt;&gt;

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:14.970
ON D-DAY.

00:01:12.468 --> 00:01:16.305
HE FOUGHT IN THE BATTLE OF THE

00:01:15.104 --> 00:01:16.638
BULGE AND HELPED LIBERATE

00:01:16.438 --> 00:01:18.107
DACHAU.

00:01:16.772 --> 00:01:20.476
&gt;&gt; JOINED BY A MAN DRAFTED AS HE

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.078
LEFT HIGH SCHOOL.

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:31.086
&gt;&gt; HE LANDED AT OMAHA BEACH ON

00:01:23.212 --> 00:01:31.687
D-DAY PLUS ONE.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.856
&gt;&gt; HAND-TO-HAND BATTLE.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:36.091
&gt;&gt; LINCOLN WAS JUST OVER 19,

00:01:33.989 --> 00:01:37.559
MANNED THE ARTILLERY AND ENTERED

00:01:36.225 --> 00:01:38.994
GOLD BEACH WITH BRITISH FORCES.

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:39.761
&gt;&gt; IT WAS IMPORTANT TO GET A

00:01:39.128 --> 00:01:42.364
FOOTHOLD.

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:42.931
FROM THEN ON, IT WAS A MATTER OF

00:01:42.498 --> 00:01:45.534
WHERE DO WE GO NEXT?

00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:47.636
&gt;&gt; AT OUR ROSE GARDEN CEREMONY,

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.171
SIGNING LEGISLATION TO HELP ALL

00:01:47.769 --> 00:01:49.771
VETERANS, PRESIDENT TRUMP

00:01:49.304 --> 00:01:50.205
REMEMBERED THE GREATEST

